### COLL008 - Bounded global growth

#### warns on an unbounded global push

- Verify: warns on an unbounded global push
   - Expected: has_code(warnings, "COLL008") is true


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: warns on an unbounded global push")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val code = "var handlers: [i64] = []\nfn add(value: i64):\n    handlers.push(value)\n"
val warnings = analyze(code)
expect(has_code(warnings, "COLL008")).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

#### accepts a dominating capacity-return guard

- Verify: accepts a dominating capacity-return guard
   - Expected: has_code(warnings, "COLL008") is false


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: accepts a dominating capacity-return guard")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val code = "var handlers: [i64] = []\nval CAP: i64 = 4\nfn add(value: i64) -> bool:\n    if handlers.len() >= CAP:\n        return false\n    handlers.push(value)\n    true\n"
val warnings = analyze(code)
expect(has_code(warnings, "COLL008")).to_equal(false)
```

</details>

#### still warns when the capacity guard follows the push

- Verify: still warns when the capacity guard follows the push
   - Expected: has_code(warnings, "COLL008") is true


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: still warns when the capacity guard follows the push")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val code = "var handlers: [i64] = []\nval CAP: i64 = 4\nfn add(value: i64) -> bool:\n    handlers.push(value)\n    if handlers.len() >= CAP:\n        return false\n    true\n"
val warnings = analyze(code)
expect(has_code(warnings, "COLL008")).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

